{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.TorusKnotTopChannelDecoration","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.TorusKnotTopChannelDecoration","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Parity"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.TorusKnotTopChannel.topChannelDecoration_two_eq_char_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.TorusKnotTopChannel.topChannelDecoration_two_eq_char_sum","kind":"theorem","line":24,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/torus-knot-top-channel-decoration.lean#L24-L30","doc":"For `m = 2` and odd `p` the top-channel decoration equals the sum of the\ntwo 2-strand Hecke characters `q^p + (−q⁻¹)^p`. (For even `p` it does not.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.TorusKnotTopChannel.topChannelDecoration","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.TorusKnotTopChannel.topChannelDecoration","kind":"def","line":18,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/torus-knot-top-channel-decoration.lean#L18-L22","doc":"The top-channel decoration `q^w − q^{−w}` at writhe `w = (m−1)p`.\nThe braid-index condition `m ≤ p` is a hypothesis on the presentation\nand is recorded in the narrative definition, not in this function. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:torus-knot-top-channel-decoration","label":"def:torus-knot-top-channel-decoration","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/torus-knot-top-channel-decoration.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}